  "findings": [
    "QN90A native root/app observed job completion medians exceed managed; native warm launch is also slightly slower.",
    "S90D native app-job admission reached 1016.031 ms and observed completion 1062.262 ms; cause is not established.",
    "Investigate job persistence/supervision/scheduling costs before the final endurance qualification; do not erase outliers by repeating trials."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Four measured pairs per TV are a bounded comparison; nearest-rank p95 equals the maximum at this sample count and does not establish a stable tail distribution.",
    "Warm fork-to-authenticated-status excludes root acquisition, service scheduling, HTTPS, app launch and boot readiness.",
    "Memory sums cover worker and native guardian at each phase. The selected managed fallback, controller and shared libraries remain present; shared mapping attribution affects PSS.",
    "CPU excludes already exited command descendants. Idle observations span approximately five seconds. Per-thread context switches are retained privately but are not wakeup counts.",
    "Descriptor/thread/mount counts are phase samples, not continuous peaks. wait4 peak RSS is not summed as a process-tree total.",
    "Job completion includes ten-millisecond polling. Nonzero exit and output were checked before forgetting; all original retained records were preserved.",
    "Kernel tails were captured around the trial, not continuously. These results do not close the full-run lifecycle evidence gate.",
    "Full acquisition/public-path performance, exact idle wakeups, continuous resource observation, recovery timing tails, 24-hour mixed endurance and power-lifecycle qualification remain open.",
    "No package update, native default switch, reboot, standby or global-policy change was performed. The .NET entry, worker fallback and independent rescue remain deployed."
  ]
